{%- comment -%}
  One brand chip. Used by the home page's "Most Loved Houses" row and by the
  A–Z cloud on the brands hub, which were identical markup in two places.

  Usage: {% render 'brand-chip', brand: brand %}

  The logo comes from the collection's own image, so a merchant sets it in
  admin (Products → Collections → the brand → Image) and it appears here with
  no theme change and no filename convention to remember. Liquid cannot test
  whether a theme asset exists, so keying off an asset name instead would print
  a broken image for every brand that has none — this way a brand without a
  logo simply renders as it does today.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign brand_name = brand.title | remove: ' Perfumes' -%}
<a class="brand-chip{% if brand.image %} has-logo{% endif %}" href="{{ brand.url }}">
  {%- if brand.image -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Two of these marks are SVG (Lattafa, Amouage) and Shopify's CDN does not
      rasterise or resize vector files, so they are served as-is; only rasters
      get a srcset. Intrinsic width/height come from the image itself rather
      than a hardcoded square — these range from 187x24 to 1328x1339, and a
      wrong ratio here would reserve the wrong box and shift the row.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign is_svg = brand.image.src | downcase | split: '?' | first | slice: -4, 4 -%}
    <img class="brand-chip-logo"
         {%- if is_svg == '.svg' %}
         src="{{ brand.image.src }}"
         {%- else %}
         src="{{ brand.image | image_url: width: 240 }}"
         srcset="{{ brand.image | image_url: width: 120 }} 120w, {{ brand.image | image_url: width: 240 }} 240w"
         sizes="76px"
         {%- endif %}
         alt="{{ brand_name | escape }}"
         width="{{ brand.image.width }}" height="{{ brand.image.height }}" loading="lazy">
  {%- endif -%}
  <span class="brand-chip-name">{{ brand_name }}</span>
  {%- if brand.products_count > 0 -%}
    <span class="brand-chip-n">{{ brand.products_count }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</a>
